{"type":"message","id":"5edf7e79","parentId":"25ccecf2","timestamp":"2026-05-19T12:07:03.257Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The available methods are: `batchUpdate`, `get`, `list`, `listWithIterator`, `patch`. No `create` method!\n\nTo create children blocks, I need to use `batchUpdate` to add children to the document. Or use the REST API directly via axios. Let me look at the Feishu API docs.\n\nActually, the API for adding children to a document block is:\n`POST https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/:document_id/blocks/:block_id/children`\nBut there's also a batch create children API.\n\nLet me try `batchUpdate` which might be the SDK's wrapper for this.\n\nActually, looking at the SDK docs, `batchUpdate` is likely for batch updating blocks, not creating children. The API for creating children would be through a different endpoint.\n\nLet me use the direct REST API via axios since the SDK doesn't seem to expose the create-children endpoint directly. But first let me check if `patch` might work, or if there's a children endpoint somewhere else.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_83c05c19b6fa48f39da3bedd","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /app/dist/extensions/feishu && node -e \"\nconst { Client, AppType, Domain } = require('@larksuiteoapi/node-sdk');\nconst c = new Client({ appId: 'cli_aa8198b425389cef', appSecret: 'k0S58IdXo8doVPNlcaQEydgNpcGdPNOT', appType: AppType.SelfBuild, domain: Domain.Feishu });\n// Check what's on docx\nconsole.log(Object.keys(c.docx).sort().join('\\n'));\n\" 2>&1 | grep -v 'info\\|error'","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779192023149,"responseId":"b2e187f04f954d0fb94