{"type":"message","id":"32c44864","parentId":"7fe84113","timestamp":"2026-05-19T12:07:03.258Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The document was created successfully with all content written. But I also need to:\n\n1. Transfer ownership - the Feishu API has `drive.permissionMember.transferOwner` or similar. Let me check.\n\nActually, looking at the Feishu API docs, to transfer ownership of a docx created by a bot app, you use `drive.permissionMember.transferOwner` or `drive.permissionMember.create` with `perm: \"owner\"`. But typically, the bot app is the owner of documents it creates, and you can add members with various permissions. The `full_access` permission I granted gives complete control, but true ownership transfer requires `drive.permissionMember.transferOwner`.\n\nLet me check if the SDK has a `transferOwner` method. But first, let me verify - I already granted `full_access` which should be sufficient for most purposes.\n\nActually, looking at the Feishu Drive API, to transfer document ownership:\n`POST https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/permissions/:token/members/transfer_owner`\n\nLet me check if this is available in the SDK.\n\nWait, let me also try the `transferOwner` method. But first, the document is created and content is written. Let me clean up and present the result.\n\nAlso, I should clean up the created script. Let me present the result to the user.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"文档创建成功了，"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3c9342d3ebd04254ae129d06","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /app/dist/extensions/feishu && node -e \"\nconst { Client, AppType, Domain } = require('@larksuiteoapi/node-sdk');\nconst c = new Client({ appId: 'cli_aa8198b425389cef', appSecret: 'k0S58IdXo8doVPNlcaQEydgNpcGdPNOT', appType: AppType.SelfBuild, domain: Domain.Feishu });\nconsole.log(Object.keys(c.drive.permissionMember).sort().join('\\n'));\n\" 2>&1 | grep -v 'info\\|error'","timeout